class:: SpectralFrameBuffer
summary:: Validate and load spectral-frame data
categories:: UGens>Buffer
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

SpectralFrameBuffer prepares deterministic ratio-and-amplitude frames for
link::Classes/SpectralFrameOsc::. It validates finite values and equal frame
sizes, optionally normalizes amplitude energy per frame, and stores data as
code::[frame][partial][ratio, amplitude]::. Metadata remains in the language
object rather than occupying undocumented Buffer samples.

classmethods::

method:: prepare

argument:: server
Destination Server. Nil selects code::Server.default::.

argument:: frameData
An array containing from 1 through 65536 frames. Each frame is
code::[ratios, amplitudes]:: and all frames must contain the same number of
partials, from 1 through 1024. Ratios must be positive and finite; amplitudes
must be finite.

argument:: normalize
When true, divide each nonzero amplitude frame by its Euclidean norm.

argument:: action
Function called asynchronously with the completed SpectralFrameBuffer object.

returns::
The Buffer allocation request. The prepared object is delivered to
code::action::.

instancemethods::

method:: buffer

returns::
The server Buffer.

method:: frames

returns::
The number of stored frames.

method:: partials

returns::
The number of partials in every frame.

method:: free

Frees the server Buffer and clears the receiver's Buffer reference.

subsection:: Discussion

Buffer loading is asynchronous. Use a Routine and code::s.sync:: before
starting a Synth. A zero-energy frame remains zero and never causes division by
zero.

examples::

code::
(
Routine({
    var ready;
    SpectralFrameBuffer.prepare(
        s,
        [
            [[1, 2, 3, 4], [1, 0.5, 0.25, 0.1]],
            [[1, 1.5, 2.7, 4], [1, 0.7, 0.2, 0.08]]
        ],
        action: { |object| ready = object }
    );
    s.sync;
    {
        SpectralFrameOsc.ar(
            ready.buffer, 80,
            frame: LFTri.kr(0.1).range(0, 1),
            frames: ready.frames, partials: ready.partials
        ) * 0.07
    }.play;
}).play;
)
::

code::
(
Routine({
    var ready;
    SpectralFrameBuffer.prepare(
        s,
        [
            [[1, 2, 4], [0, 0, 0]],
            [[1, 3, 5], [1, 0.3, 0.1]]
        ],
        false,
        { |object| ready = object }
    );
    s.sync;
    ready.frames.postln;
    ready.partials.postln;
}).play;
)
::

